  dawtool, abletoolz's Live 12 fixtures; see libmscore/liveset.h). The test gzips it into an .als.
  UNVERIFIED until the owner's own Live 12 file is tried: in particular the MIDI input routing of a
  single port and channel (only Live's default "MidiIn/External.All/-1" / "Ext: All Ins" is known)
  and what the CurveControl attributes mean. Not a file made by Live.

  Track "Strings 1": MIDI from "MuseScore A", channel 1 (the Violin part's route), Kontakt with
    Vibrato automated (a ramp, then a curve, then a point in the repeat's second pass and one after it),
    an "Unknown Knob" nothing maps to, the mixer's volume, and a looped MIDI clip at beats 8-16 whose
    envelope ramps CC 21 over its 4-beat loop.
  Track "Flute": all inputs (matched by name), a Kontakt slot named "#002 Tone" stepping 0 -> 1.
-->
